=============================================================================
OPT-IN `vst3-gpl` FEATURE: GPLv3
=============================================================================
Building with `--features vst3-gpl` links nih-plug's VST3 wrapper, which uses
vst3-sys (https://github.com/robbert-vdh/vst3-sys), licensed GPLv3.
Binaries built this way must be distributed under GPLv3, with source.
Nusick's own source code stays MIT. Official Nusick releases never enable
this feature.

Steinberg's VST3 SDK headers are themselves MIT-licensed as of 2025, but
vst3-sys keeps its own GPLv3 license. A future Nusick VST3 wrapper built on
the MIT/Apache `vst3` crate (https://github.com/coupler-rs/vst3-rs) will
remove this restriction.
